#: ../../../ros_installation.md:54
msgid "Installing the Default Gazebo/ROS Pairing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:56
msgid ""
"If you are planning on using a specific version of ROS and don't have a "
"reason to use a specific version of Gazebo, we recommend using the default "
"version of Gazebo available from the ROS repository when installing "
"`ros_gz`. You can find  instructions on adding the ROS repository to your "
"system in the  [ROS documentation](https://docs.ros.org/en/humble/"
"Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup.html#add-the-ros-2-apt-"
"repository).  The following command will install the correct version of "
"Gazebo and `ros_gz`  for your ROS installation on a Linux system. You should "
"replace `${ROS_DISTRO}`  with your ROS distribution (e.g. `humble`, "
"`rolling`, `noetic`, etc)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:65
msgid "sudo apt-get install ros-${ROS_DISTRO}-ros-gz\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:69
msgid ""
"This command will install the Gazebo libraries recommended for your ROS "
"installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:72
msgid "ROS 2 Gazebo Vendor packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:74
msgid ""
"As of ROS 2 Jazzy, Gazebo is available from the ROS package repository via "
"vendor packages. If your package directly depends on a Gazebo library, "
"instead of relying only on `ros_gz`, refer to [this documentation]"
"(ros2_gz_vendor_pkgs) to learn how to use the Gazebo vendor packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:80
msgid ""
"<div class=\"warning\">\n"
"The rest of this document provides more information and other, alternative,\n"
"installations pathways. We do not recommend the following approaches for "
"new\n"
"users.\n"
"</div>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:86
msgid "Specific ROS and Gazebo Pairings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:88
msgid ""
"Gazebo is an independent project like Boost, Ogre, and many other projects "
"used by ROS. Usually, the latest version of Gazebo is available at the "
"beginning of each ROS release cycle (for example Gazebo Fortress for ROS 2 "
"Humble). This version of Gazebo is selected as the official Gazebo release "
"for that ROS Distro and is fully integrated, tested, and supported for the "
"life of the ROS distribution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:95
msgid ""
"Note that all Gazebo libraries follow the [semantic versioning](http://"
"semver.org/) philosophy for ABI stability. All Gazebo versions that have the "
"same major number (`gz-sim7_7.0.0`, `gz-sim7_7.1.0`, `gz-sim7_7.0.1`, ...) "
"are binary compatible and thus interchangeable with a given ROS distro."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:101
msgid "Installing Gazebo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:103
msgid "Gazebo Packages for Ubuntu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:105
msgid ""
"The easiest way of installing Gazebo on Ubuntu is to use binary packages. "
"There are two main repositories that host Gazebo simulator and Gazebo "
"libraries: one is `packages.ros.org` and the other is the Gazebo repository "
"known as [`packages.osrfoundation.org`](https://packages.osrfoundation.org/"
"gazebo/ubuntu/). At the time of writing the following packages are available "
"on the following hosts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:111
msgid "**packages.ros.org**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:112
msgid "ROS 2 Humble: Gazebo Fortress"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:113
msgid "ROS 2 Jazzy: Gazebo Harmonic (ROS vendor packages)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:114
msgid "ROS 2 Kilted: Gazebo Ionic (ROS vendor packages)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:115
msgid "ROS 2 Lyrical: Gazebo Jetty (ROS vendor packages)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:116
msgid "ROS 2 Rolling: Gazebo Jetty (ROS vendor packages, changing frequently)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:118
msgid "**packages.osrfoundation.org**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:119
msgid "Gazebo Fortress"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:120
msgid "Gazebo Harmonic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:121
msgid "Gazebo Ionic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:122
msgid "Gazebo Jetty"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:124
msgid ""
"This means that including the `osrfoundation.org` repository is not strictly "
"needed to get the Gazebo binary packages, as it can be installed from the "
"ROS repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:128
msgid "Installing Non-Default Gazebo/ROS 2 Pairings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:130
msgid ""
"Only use this approach if you absolutely need to run a version of Gazebo "
"that is not officially supported by your ROS distro. Using this approach "
"will make it impossible to use the official ROS Ubuntu packages that depend "
"on Gazebo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:135
msgid "We do not recommend this approach for beginners!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:138
msgid ""
"To select a different release of Gazebo than the one officially supported by "
"your ROS distribution you must either **use non ROS official Gazebo binary "
"packages** or **manually compile** [`ros_gz`](https://github.com/gazebosim/"
"ros_gz) from source (this rule applies for every ROS package that uses a "
"Gazebo library):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:144
msgid ""
"**Use non ROS official ros_gz binary packages:** `packages.osrfoundation."
"org` provides binary packages for `ros_gz` for some combinations of Gazebo "
"and ROS that are different from the officially supported combination. In "
"some circumstances the non-official packages can be outdated or even buggy, "
"the use of them is reserved for advanced users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:149
msgid ""
"**Manually compile ros_gz:** some combinations of Gazebo and ROS can be "
"prepared to be built together but have no binary packages, neither in "
"`packages.ros.org` or `packages.osrfoundation.org`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:152
msgid ""
"Both approaches may also require that you modify your ROS or Gazebo source "
"code to support this compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:154
msgid "📦 Gazebo Harmonic with ROS 2 Humble"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:156
msgid ""
"Gazebo Harmonic can be used with ROS 2 Humble and non ROS official binary "
"packages hosted in `packages.osrfoundation.org`. These packages conflict "
"with `ros-humble-ros-gz*` packages (Humble officially supports Gazebo "
"Fortress)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:160
msgid "To install the binary Gazebo Harmonic/ROS 2 Humble packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:162
msgid ""
"Follow [these instruction to install gz-harmonic](https://gazebosim.org/docs/"
"harmonic/install_ubuntu#binary-installation-on-ubuntu) from [`packages."
"osrfoundation.org`](https://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo/ubuntu/) "
"repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:165
msgid "Install `ros_gz` from the non official binary packages from apt:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:166
msgid "`apt-get install ros-humble-ros-gzharmonic`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:168
msgid "Using the Latest Gazebo Source Code for a Gazebo Distribution"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:170
msgid ""
"The Gazebo team usually backports and releases new versions of each of the "
"supported Gazebo releases and libraries (i.e: bumping `gz-sim 7.0.0` to gz-"
"sim `7.1.0`). These updates are hosted first in the `packages.osrfoundation."
"org` repository. The ROS repository syncs from the `osrfoundation.org` "
"repository frequently but versions can be different."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:176
msgid ""
"Getting the latest versions of the Gazebo libraries and simulator is as easy "
"as installing the [`osrfoundation.org` repository](install_ubuntu_src."
"md#install-dependencies) together with the ROS repository. Updates should be "
"fully compatible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:180
msgid "FAQ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:182
msgid "I am not using ROS at all, which version should I use?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:184
msgid ""
"If you don't need ROS support, the recommended version is the latest "
"released version that can be [installed using the `osrfoundation.org` repo]"
"(https://gazebosim.org/docs) depending on your platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:188
msgid "I want to use Gazebo Harmonic with ROS 2. Where are the packages?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:190
msgid ""
"We provide binary packages for `ros_gz` for the following Gazebo and ROS 2 "
"pairings in the packages.osrfoundation.org repository but these packages are "
"not official ROS packages, which means if there is a breaking change in the "
"corresponding ROS 2 distribution, there will be a short delay before these "
"packages are rebuilt with the changes. Installing these packages may also "
"cause conflicts with other ROS packages that depend on Gazebo-classic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:0
msgid "**Gazebo Harmonic (LTS)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:0
msgid "`ros-humble-ros-gzharmonic`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:201
msgid ""
"What is the difference between a ROS vendor package and other packages "
"listed in this  page?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:203
msgid ""
"The ROS vendor packages are (indeed) ROS packages (built by the ROS "
"buildfarm and hosted in the ROS repository) that provide the installation of "
"the Gazebo librariess. In this page, unless mentioned the vendor in the "
"name, the rest of packages are standard debian packages the ones installed "
"by the package manager (usually apt)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:207
msgid ""
"Where I can find the different features implemented on each Gazebo version?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:209
msgid ""
"The best place is the Gazebo web page that hosts a list of the [main "
"features available in each Gazebo distribution](release-features)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:212
msgid ""
"Some notes are regularly posted on the [Gazebo community site](https://"
"community.gazebosim.org/tags/c/release-announcements-and-discussions/10/"
"release) and special posts and videos are also posted there when a new "
"release is out: See the one for [Garden](https://community.gazebosim.org/t/"
"gazebo-garden-release/1627) or the one for [Fortress](https://community."
"gazebosim.org/t/ignition-fortress-release/1127) as examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros_installation.md:221
msgid ""
"Additionally, when navigating through the different versions of Gazebo there "
"is a menu item called \"[Feature Comparison](comparison)\" which provides a "
"comparison with the features of Gazebo-Classic. In the top right corner of "
"the [Gazebo documentation page](https://gazebosim.org/docs) the specific "
"Gazebo version to compare with can be selected."
msgstr ""
